    "p2_head_criterion_reason": "v_(1-i)((i;i)_j) is capped at 4 because (i;i)_4 = 0; four of the five atoms have v(head) >= 4, so no j can catch them. Only the neutron (v(head) = 2) fires.",
    "p2_closed_by_direct_evaluation": true,
    "p2_direct_evaluation_reason": "p=2 is a single prime and (i;i)_4 = 0 truncates the sum after four terms, whose coefficients every atom has on disk, so Frob_2 = P(i)/denom(i) is a finite exact computation in Z[i]. Frob_2 = -2^(1-2M) with M = Z+N, verified on every (Z,N) with Z+N <= 6 — never zero. P(i) = P(-1) = A, so one integer runs both p=2 and the odd primes.",
